1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,730
There are trends in food, much as there are trends in clothing.

2
00:00:05,730 --> 00:00:11,790
Interest in food fashions has risen rapidly since the birth of the smartphone

3
00:00:12,151 --> 00:00:16,586
when people first began taking photos of their food

4
00:00:16,586 --> 00:00:20,040
and instantly sharing them with their friends.

5
00:00:20,040 --> 00:00:23,220
The food industry in the UK, in particular

6
00:00:23,220 --> 00:00:30,480
is obsessed with finding and exploiting the next big food trend.

7
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:35,360
Marketeers aim to create a huge demand for a food item

8
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:40,240
which was previously unknown, or not needed.

9
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:50,230
One of the most effective ways of promoting a new food product is by using social media influencers as brand ambassadors.

10
00:00:50,230 --> 00:00:52,520
In return for free samples

11
00:00:52,520 --> 00:00:58,686
many influencers will post content about a product, although there are influencers

12
00:00:58,686 --> 00:01:01,620
with hundreds of thousands of followers

13
00:01:01,620 --> 00:01:05,650
who can command large fees for their services.

14
00:01:05,650 --> 00:01:15,510
Companies which sell vegan produce were pioneers in being able to increase sales really quickly in this way.

15
00:01:15,510 --> 00:01:21,525
For a food item to become really popular it has to be readily available,

16
00:01:21,525 --> 00:01:27,110
so supermarkets have a role to play in creating a new food trend.

17
00:01:27,110 --> 00:01:30,500
They have dedicated teams closely following

18
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:35,424
which new products or ingredients are trending on social media

19
00:01:35,424 --> 00:01:42,180
and are particularly interested in what well-known chefs are putting on their menus.

20
00:01:42,180 --> 00:01:47,411
I'd like to look at a few examples of marketing campaigns

21
00:01:47,411 --> 00:01:51,770
which were really successful in launching a new fashion trend.

22
00:01:51,770 --> 00:01:56,320
Starting in the 1990s with the avocado.

23
00:01:56,320 --> 00:02:02,900
A British PR company was hired to raise its profile and stimulate demand.

24
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:11,430
They paid for a group of journalists to travel out to South Africa to meet avocado farmers.

25
00:02:11,430 --> 00:02:18,705
Articles written following this visit helped to educate the British public about the avocado,

26
00:02:18,705 --> 00:02:25,980
which at this time was certainly not the daily staple it's since become.

27
00:02:25,980 --> 00:02:32,013
Advertisements were designed to promote the avocado as a 'superfood':

28
00:02:32,013 --> 00:02:36,840
rich in nutrients and therefore beneficial for health.

29
00:02:36,840 --> 00:02:51,221
Avocados became hugely fashionable and within a few years UK avocado sales had grown from 13 million pounds annually to around 150 million,

30
00:02:51,221 --> 00:02:59,350
making it one of the most successful fresh produce campaigns in UK history.

31
00:02:59,350 --> 00:03:06,860
Oat milk is a recent example of a new product which became fashionable very quickly.

32
00:03:06,860 --> 00:03:10,880
Now there are many brands available, but one company

33
00:03:10,880 --> 00:03:16,670
which had early success was the Swedish brand, Oatly.

34
00:03:16,670 --> 00:03:19,375
They attracted a lot of attention

35
00:03:19,375 --> 00:03:26,590
with a media campaign which used provocation as a way of getting their message across effectively.

36
00:03:26,590 --> 00:03:35,626
The fact that this campaign aggravated competitors producing milk from dairy cows was seen as a plus,

37
00:03:35,626 --> 00:03:40,410
as it helped to make oat milk seem cool.

38
00:03:40,410 --> 00:03:50,024
In the USA, the brand decided against a big retail launch in favour of getting the product into coffee chains,

39
00:03:50,024 --> 00:03:54,350
which removed the need for a big advertising budget.

40
00:03:54,350 --> 00:04:00,560
This proved far more effective than offering samples in supermarkets.

41
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:07,800
Oat milk had an advantage over other alternative milk products such as almond milk.

42
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:14,080
Many consumers prefer it because it has less of an impact on the environment.

43
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:21,331
It requires significantly less water to produce than other alternative milk products

44
00:04:21,331 --> 00:04:26,770
and it also has a relatively low carbon footprint.

45
00:04:26,770 --> 00:04:31,320
Norwegian skrei, a rarely available seasonal fish delicacy,

46
00:04:31,320 --> 00:04:34,480
otherwise known as Arctic cod

47
00:04:34,820 --> 00:04:40,990
is now found on the menus of Michelin starred restaurants throughout Europe.

48
00:04:40,990 --> 00:04:51,060
The demand for skrei has been used by a food marketing agency to build the reputation of Norway's fisheries in general.

49
00:04:51,060 --> 00:05:00,660
Marketing surveys have shown that a significant number of shoppers now associate Norway with excellent seafood.

50
00:05:00,660 --> 00:05:11,240
Food trends can be considered a good thing in some ways as they can benefit farmers and food producers enormously.

51
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:18,010
The public can also be encouraged to buy things which are more sustainably produced.

52
00:05:18,010 --> 00:05:25,412
But ethical concerns have been raised about the effects a surge in demand can cause.

53
00:05:25,412 --> 00:05:27,880
Quinoa is a classic example.

54
00:05:27,880 --> 00:05:31,068
This plant is native to Peru,

55
00:05:31,068 --> 00:05:35,600
and when demand peaked some years ago, the price soared

56
00:05:35,600 --> 00:05:39,570
making it unaffordable for local people.

57
00:05:39,570 --> 00:05:43,980
While the popularity of quinoa has benefitted farmers financially

58
00:05:43,980 --> 00:05:48,060
there have been other negative consequences.

59
00:05:48,060 --> 00:05:56,500
As demand grew, farmers began working the land all year round in order to produce more quinoa.

60
00:05:56,500 --> 00:06:03,334
One issue has been that the fertility of the soil decreased dramatically,

61
00:06:03,334 --> 00:06:08,460
which could potentially lead to desertification in some areas.

